      "value": "@{62e03f4e44af5544b2228fa5|full_name} this argument doesn't make any sense. In the end, it doesn't matter WHO gives VRC money - they received money tied to your account and it should qualify you for an age verification. Continuing subscription is also irrelevant - as it stands, if you pay one time, do the age verification, then cancel your Plus subscription, your age verification does NOT go away (and it shouldn't! That would just be a waste). All this canny is saying is anyone with a recent history of having had Plus should qualify for an age verification. How far back you'd qualify could be up for debate, but I agree with the OP.",
