      "value": "@{62e03f4e44af5544b2228fa5|full_name}\n\nThis whole angle you're taking about \"trusting the platform\" by personally paying for VRChat Plus just doesn't hold up under scrutiny. You're acting like age verification is some kind of spiritual bond between a user and the company, when in reality it's just a paid service tied to an account. That's it. The only thing that matters is whether the platform got paid to process the verification.\n\nIf someone gifts a sub to another user, VRChat still gets the money. The account receiving the gift still ends up associated with a payment. Trying to draw a line between \"self-paid\" and \"gifted\" is arbitrary and meaningless from both a technical and financial perspective. You're creating a moral distinction where there is none.\n\nAnd let’s really get into the logic of this. Are you saying a user who *wants* to be age verified but can’t afford a subscription should just be excluded unless they personally fund the payment? That’s not just elitist, it’s bad community policy. Plenty of legit users rely on gifted subs. That doesn’t make them less real, less trustworthy, or less deserving of access to age-restricted spaces.\n\nAlso, your argument about \"users staying on the platform longer\" because they bought a sub themselves is a stretch. Newsflash: a gifted sub still gives the platform a financial incentive to keep that user around. You're not magically more loyal because you personally swiped the card.\n\nThe system should be simple. If an account has had VRChat Plus, regardless of how it was acquired, it should be eligible to register for age verification. That creates a fair path for more people to get verified without jumping through financial purity hoops.\n\nThis isn’t about vibes. It’s about function. And your version of gatekeeping helps no one.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
